  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $5.5B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury recorded 7,370 awards with an average award size of $747K. Obligations fell 35.7% year over year. Historical totals show declining but variable spending: FY21 was $9.6B, FY22 was $9.3B, FY23 was $10.3B, FY24 was $9.3B, and FY25 was $8.6B. The top NAICS categories concentrate spending in metals and information technology: Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining accounted for $1.2B and Other Computer Related Services accounted for $1B. The contract roster is led by large vendors concentrated in metals refining and IT services. STONEX FINANCIAL LTD received $1B, and ASAHI REFINING USA INC received $494M. The Department of the Treasury’s FY2026 to date profile shows fewer obligations and a shift in mix toward high-dollar metal processing and computer-related services while overall fiscal-year-to-date totals remain partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How much did Treasury obligate in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $5.5B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury executed 7,370 awards with an average award size of $747K. Obligations fell 35.7% year over year. The Department of the Treasury’s FY21 through FY25 annual obligations were $9.6B, $9.3B, $10.3B, $9.3B, and $8.6B respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest spending categories and vendors so far in FY2026?",
        "body": "Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining is the largest NAICS category at $1.2B, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $1B and Computer Systems Design Services at $609M. STONEX FINANCIAL LTD is the largest vendor at $1B, followed by ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $494M and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $267M. Metals processing and IT services dominate the top categories and top vendors lists."
      }
    ]
