      "q": "How much does Department of the Treasury spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $5.5B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury recorded 7,370 awards with an average award size of $747K. Obligations fell 35.7% year over year. FY21 through FY25 totals were $9.6B, $9.3B, $10.3B, $9.3B, and $8.6B respectively."
